{
  "id": "asleep-in-the-deep",
  "version": 2,
  "reviewed": true,
  "title": "Asleep in the Deep",
  "description": "H. W. Petrie's 1897 bass showpiece, for 2 to 4 singers: the bass sings the tune and the words, from the stormy verse to the famous falling \"Beware!\", while the alto, soprano and tenor hold soft chords on \"oo\" above it, on Petrie's own harmony. A rolling, dramatic sea song. A stretch song: its tune runs from a low F to a high D, wider than a beginner bass's comfortable range, so take the top and bottom notes gently.",
  "language": "en",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "genre": [
    "parlour song",
    "bass solo"
  ],
  "style": "free",
  "tempo": 60,
  "key": "F",
  "timeSignature": "6/8",
  "pickupBeats": 0,
  "credits": {
    "words": "Arthur J. Lamb (1897)",
    "tune": "H. W. Petrie (1897)",
    "arrangement": "Stackapella, on Petrie's harmony"
  },
  "licence": {
    "words": "public domain: Lamb died 1928",
    "tune": "public domain: Petrie died 1925",
    "arrangement": "original, written for Stackapella on Petrie's piano harmony (public domain): the tune in the bass as he wrote it, with breaths written in for beginners, and the other three parts on \"oo\"",
    "recordings": "synthesized guides",
    "checked": null,
    "source": "\"Asleep in the Deep\", song for baritone or bass voice, words by Arthur J. Lamb, music by H. W. Petrie (New York: F. A. Mills; first published 1897, this printing captioned \"Copyright, 1901, by F. A. Mills\"), in F with the voice in treble clef, sung an octave lower; read from the scan in the Lester S. Levy Sheet Music Collection, Johns Hopkins University, Box 145, Item 046 (levysheetmusic.mse.jhu.edu/collection/145/046), and checked against M. Witmark & Sons' edition in D (IMSLP 191240). Verse 1 and the refrain, in Mills's words; the 12/8 written as 6/8; the fermatas and the ad lib. bar sung as written; the small slide note into the last \"ware!\" left out"
  },
